id: grok-adapter
order: 5
description: "Use xAI Grok models with TanStack AI — Grok 4.3, Grok Build 0.1, Grok Imagine image generation, and Grok Imagine video generation via @tanstack/ai-grok."
keywords:
  - tanstack ai
  - grok
  - xai
  - grok 4.3
  - grok build
  - image generation
  - video generation
  - grok imagine
  - adapter
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Grok text and summarization adapters provide access to xAI's Responses API for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grok-4.3"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grok-build-0.1"},{"type":"text","value":", plus Grok Imagine image generation and Grok Imagine video generation."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"installation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Installation"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"react\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-grok\"]],\"vue\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-grok\"]],\"solid\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-grok\"]],\"svelte\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-grok\"]],\"preact\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-grok\"]],\"angular\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-grok\"]],\"vanilla\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-grok\"]],\"octane\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-grok\"]]},\"mode\":\"install\"}"}},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"basic-usage","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Basic Usage"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { grokText } from \"@tanstack/ai-grok\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: grokText(\"grok-build-0.1\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello!\" }],\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"basic-usage-custom-api-key","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Basic Usage - Custom API Key"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { createGrokText } from \"@tanstack/ai-grok\";\n\nconst adapter = createGrokText(\"grok-build-0.1\", process.env.XAI_API_KEY!);\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter,\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello!\" }],\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"configuration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Configuration"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createGrokText, type GrokTextConfig } from \"@tanstack/ai-grok\";\n\nconst config: Omit<GrokTextConfig, \"apiKey\"> = {\n  baseURL: \"https://api.x.ai/v1\", // Optional, this is the default\n};\n\nconst adapter = createGrokText(\"grok-build-0.1\", process.env.XAI_API_KEY!, config);","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"grok-on-vertex","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Grok on Vertex"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-grok/vertex"},{"type":"text","value":" when Grok must run on Vertex AI. That path\nuses Google Cloud credentials and Vertex regional or global endpoints."}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"react\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-grok\",\"google-auth-library\"]],\"vue\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-grok\",\"google-auth-library\"]],\"solid\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-grok\",\"google-auth-library\"]],\"svelte\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-grok\",\"google-auth-library\"]],\"preact\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-grok\",\"google-auth-library\"]],\"angular\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-grok\",\"google-auth-library\"]],\"vanilla\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-grok\",\"google-auth-library\"]],\"octane\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-grok\",\"google-auth-library\"]]},\"mode\":\"install\"}"}},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { grokVertexText } from \"@tanstack/ai-grok/vertex\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: grokVertexText(\"grok-4.3\", {\n    project: \"my-project\",\n    location: \"global\",\n  }),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello!\" }],\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"project"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"location"},{"type":"text","value":" use the same names as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-vertex"},{"type":"text","value":". If you\nomit "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"location"},{"type":"text","value":", the factory uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"global"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grokVertexText"},{"type":"text","value":" accepts only the Grok chat models that Vertex lists:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grok-4.3"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grok-4.20-reasoning"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grok-4.20-non-reasoning"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grok-4.1-fast-reasoning"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grok-4.1-fast-non-reasoning"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"xAI API models such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grok-4.6"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grok-build-0.1"},{"type":"text","value":" are not on Vertex."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The adapter sends the Vertex model id "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"xai/grok-4.3"},{"type":"text","value":". Install\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"google-auth-library"},{"type":"text","value":" for Application Default Credentials, or pass\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"authClient"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getAccessToken"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grokVertexSummarize"},{"type":"text","value":" from the same entry when you need summarize on\nVertex."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Gemini on Vertex lives in "},{"type":"link","href":"./vertex","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-vertex"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example-chat-completion","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example: Chat Completion"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { grokText } from \"@tanstack/ai-grok\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json();\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: grokText(\"grok-build-0.1\"),\n    messages,\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example-with-tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example: With Tools"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse, toolDefinition } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { grokText } from \"@tanstack/ai-grok\";\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\n\nconst getWeatherDef = toolDefinition({\n  name: \"get_weather\",\n  description: \"Get the current weather\",\n  inputSchema: z.object({\n    location: z.string(),\n  }),\n});\n\nconst getWeather = getWeatherDef.server(async ({ location }) => {\n  // Fetch weather data\n  return { temperature: 72, conditions: \"sunny\" };\n});\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json();\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: grokText(\"grok-build-0.1\"),\n    messages,\n    tools: [getWeather],\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"model-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Model Options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Grok supports xAI Responses API options. Sampling parameters live here too — "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"temperature"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"top_p"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"max_output_tokens"},{"type":"text","value":" — rather than as root-level props on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { grokText } from \"@tanstack/ai-grok\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json();\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: grokText(\"grok-build-0.1\"),\n    messages,\n    modelOptions: {\n      temperature: 0.7,\n      top_p: 0.9,\n      max_output_tokens: 1024,\n      store: false,\n      include: [\"reasoning.encrypted_content\"],\n    },\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you previously passed "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"temperature"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"topP"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maxTokens"},{"type":"text","value":" at the root of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":", see "},{"type":"link","href":"../migration/sampling-options-to-model-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Moving Sampling Options into modelOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"summarization","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Summarization"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Summarize long text content:"}]},{"type":"html","value":"<!-- ignored: grokSummarize()'s resolved provider-options type sits in a\n     contravariant position in SummarizeAdapter, so it isn't assignable to\n     summarize()'s adapter param for any current Grok model. Tracked in #821;\n     un-ignore once the adapter type is corrected. -->"},{"type":"code","value":"import { summarize } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { grokSummarize } from \"@tanstack/ai-grok\";\n\nconst result = await summarize({\n  adapter: grokSummarize(\"grok-4.3\"),\n  text: \"Your long text to summarize...\",\n  maxLength: 100,\n  style: \"concise\", // \"concise\" | \"bullet-points\" | \"paragraph\"\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.summary);","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"image-generation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Image Generation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Generate images with a Grok Imagine model."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The image models ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grok-imagine-image"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grok-imagine-image-2.0"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grok-imagine-image-quality"},{"type":"text","value":") are aspect-ratio sized — "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"size"},{"type":"text","value":" takes an\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aspectRatio_resolution"},{"type":"text","value":" template like "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"16:9_2k\""},{"type":"text","value":" (the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"_2k"},{"type":"text","value":" suffix is\noptional). "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grok-imagine-image-2.0"},{"type":"text","value":" is xAI's recommended model and adds a\n2.0-only "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"quality"},{"type":"text","value":" provider option ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'low' | 'medium'"},{"type":"text","value":", default "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'medium'"},{"type":"text","value":"):"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { grokImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-grok\";\n\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: grokImage(\"grok-imagine-image-2.0\"),\n  prompt: \"A futuristic cityscape at sunset\",\n  size: \"16:9_2k\",\n  modelOptions: { quality: \"medium\" },\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"image-editing-image-to-image","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Image Editing (image-to-image)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The grok-imagine models accept image prompt parts for image-conditioned\ngeneration via xAI's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/v1/images/edits"},{"type":"text","value":" endpoint — up to 3 source images,\naddressed by xAI in the order they appear in the prompt. Per xAI's docs\nthere is no in-prompt referencing syntax; write the prompt naturally and\nyour text is sent verbatim:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { grokImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-grok\";\n\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: grokImage(\"grok-imagine-image\"),\n  prompt: [\n    {\n      type: \"text\",\n      content: \"Render the product in the style of the second image\",\n    },\n    {\n      type: \"image\",\n      source: { type: \"url\", value: \"https://example.com/product.png\" },\n    },\n    {\n      type: \"image\",\n      source: { type: \"url\", value: \"https://example.com/style.png\" },\n    },\n  ],\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"URL sources are fetched by xAI's servers, so they must be publicly\nreachable; use a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data"},{"type":"text","value":" source for private images."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"video-generation-experimental","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Video Generation (Experimental)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Generate short video clips (1–15 seconds, with audio) with the Grok Imagine video models via xAI's asynchronous jobs/polling API."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Available models:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grok-imagine-video"},{"type":"text","value":" (v1.0) — text-to-video, image-to-video, and source-video edit / extend, $0.05 per second of video."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grok-imagine-video-1.5"},{"type":"text","value":" — xAI's recommended default, $0.08 per second of video. Supports text-to-video (with native 1080p), image-to-video, and reference-to-video. It does not accept a source video."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Text-to-video:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateVideo, getVideoJobStatus } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { grokVideo } from \"@tanstack/ai-grok\";\n\nconst adapter = grokVideo(\"grok-imagine-video-1.5\");\n\n// 1. Create the job\nconst { jobId } = await generateVideo({\n  adapter,\n  prompt: \"A red panda balancing on a bamboo stalk in the rain\",\n  size: \"16:9_720p\", // \"aspectRatio\" or \"aspectRatio_resolution\"\n  duration: 5, // integer seconds, 1–15\n});\n\n// 2. Poll until complete, then read the video URL\nlet status = await getVideoJobStatus({ adapter, jobId });\nwhile (status.status !== \"completed\" && status.status !== \"failed\") {\n  await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, 5000));\n  status = await getVideoJobStatus({ adapter, jobId });\n}\n\nconsole.log(status.url); // hosted .mp4 URL","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For image-to-video, include an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"image"},{"type":"text","value":" prompt part as the starting frame and describe the desired motion in the text part. URL sources are fetched by xAI's servers (so they must be publicly reachable); use a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data"},{"type":"text","value":" source for a base64 starting frame:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateVideo } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { grokVideo } from \"@tanstack/ai-grok\";\n\nconst { jobId } = await generateVideo({\n  adapter: grokVideo(\"grok-imagine-video-1.5\"),\n  prompt: [\n    {\n      type: \"text\",\n      content: \"Make the waterfall crash down and slowly pan out the camera\",\n    },\n    {\n      type: \"image\",\n      source: { type: \"url\", value: \"https://example.com/waterfall-still.png\" },\n    },\n  ],\n  size: \"16:9_720p\",\n  duration: 10,\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Like the Grok Imagine image models, sizing is aspect-ratio based: the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"size"},{"type":"text","value":" option takes an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aspectRatio_resolution"},{"type":"text","value":" template. Supported aspect ratios are "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"1:1"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"16:9"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"9:16"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"4:3"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"3:4"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"3:2"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"2:3"},{"type":"text","value":"; supported resolutions are "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"480p"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"720p"},{"type":"text","value":", and (on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grok-imagine-video-1.5"},{"type":"text","value":" text-to-video / image-to-video only) "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"1080p"},{"type":"text","value":" (e.g. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"9:16_1080p\""},{"type":"text","value":"). The resolution suffix is optional."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"reference-to-video","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reference-to-Video"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grok-imagine-video-1.5"},{"type":"text","value":", image prompt parts with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metadata.role: 'reference'"},{"type":"text","value":" (or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'character'"},{"type":"text","value":") become "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reference_images"},{"type":"text","value":" — they guide subjects and style without locking the first frame, and are addressed from the prompt text as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<IMAGE_0>"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<IMAGE_1>"},{"type":"text","value":", … in request order. Preset TTS voices (up to 3) can be referenced for generated speech via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions.reference_audios"},{"type":"text","value":", addressed as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<AUDIO_0>"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<AUDIO_1>"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<AUDIO_2>"},{"type":"text","value":". Reference-to-video output is capped at 720p. A starting-frame image can be combined with reference inputs on 1.5: the start frame pins the opening frame while the references steer subjects, style, and voices. Reference inputs are a 1.5-only feature, so the adapter rejects them on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grok-imagine-video"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateVideo } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { grokVideo } from \"@tanstack/ai-grok\";\n\nconst { jobId } = await generateVideo({\n  adapter: grokVideo(\"grok-imagine-video-1.5\"),\n  prompt: [\n    {\n      type: \"text\",\n      content: \"<IMAGE_0> walks through a neon-lit alley while <AUDIO_0> narrates\",\n    },\n    {\n      type: \"image\",\n      source: { type: \"url\", value: \"https://example.com/opening-frame.png\" },\n      metadata: { role: \"start_frame\" },\n    },\n    {\n      type: \"image\",\n      source: { type: \"url\", value: \"https://example.com/character.png\" },\n      metadata: { role: \"reference\" },\n    },\n  ],\n  size: \"16:9_720p\",\n  modelOptions: {\n    reference_audios: [{ voice_id: \"eve\" }],\n  },\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"video-editing-and-extension","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Video Editing and Extension"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grok-imagine-video"},{"type":"text","value":" (v1.0) can rewrite or continue an existing clip. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grok-imagine-video-1.5"},{"type":"text","value":" has no video input — the adapter rejects a source-video part or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mode"},{"type":"text","value":" on that model. Pass the source clip as a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"video"},{"type":"text","value":" prompt part and pick the mode with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions.mode"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mode: 'edit'"},{"type":"text","value":" posts to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/v1/videos/edits"},{"type":"text","value":" — modifies only what the prompt asks for, keeping the rest of the clip intact. Duration, aspect ratio, and resolution are inherited from the source (capped at 720p), so the adapter rejects "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"size"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aspect_ratio"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resolution"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"duration"},{"type":"text","value":" in this mode rather than sending fields the API ignores."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mode: 'extend'"},{"type":"text","value":" posts to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/v1/videos/extensions"},{"type":"text","value":" — continues the clip. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"duration"},{"type":"text","value":" is the length of the "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"added tail"}]},{"type":"text","value":", not the total: extending a 10-second clip with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"duration: 5"},{"type":"text","value":" yields 15 seconds. Output geometry is still inherited from the source, so "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"size"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aspect_ratio"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resolution"},{"type":"text","value":" are rejected here too."}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateVideo } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { grokVideo } from \"@tanstack/ai-grok\";\n\nconst adapter = grokVideo(\"grok-imagine-video\");\n\n// Edit: change the clip in place\nconst edit = await generateVideo({\n  adapter,\n  prompt: [\n    { type: \"text\", content: \"Make the sky stormy with distant lightning\" },\n    {\n      type: \"video\",\n      source: { type: \"url\", value: \"https://example.com/clip.mp4\" },\n    },\n  ],\n  modelOptions: { mode: \"edit\" },\n});\n\n// Extend: append 5 more seconds\nconst extension = await generateVideo({\n  adapter,\n  prompt: [\n    { type: \"text\", content: \"The camera keeps panning right across the bay\" },\n    {\n      type: \"video\",\n      source: { type: \"url\", value: \"https://example.com/clip.mp4\" },\n    },\n  ],\n  duration: 5, // added seconds, not the total\n  modelOptions: { mode: \"extend\" },\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Both return the usual "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ jobId }"},{"type":"text","value":" and are polled like any other Grok video job."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When the job completes, the adapter reports usage on the result: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"usage.billed"},{"type":"text","value":" carries the billed seconds of video ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ quantity, unit: 'seconds' }"},{"type":"text","value":") and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"usage.cost"},{"type":"text","value":" the exact cost in USD, both as returned by the xAI API."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See "},{"type":"link","href":"../media/video-generation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Video Generation"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for the full jobs/polling flow, streaming mode, and the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useGenerateVideo"},{"type":"text","value":" hook."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"text-to-speech","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Text-to-Speech"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Generate speech with Grok TTS:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateSpeech } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { grokSpeech } from \"@tanstack/ai-grok\";\n\nconst result = await generateSpeech({\n  adapter: grokSpeech(\"grok-tts\"),\n  text: \"Hello from Grok!\",\n  voice: \"default\",\n  format: \"mp3\",\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.audio); // Base64-encoded audio","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"transcription","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Transcription"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Transcribe audio with Grok STT:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateTranscription } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { grokTranscription } from \"@tanstack/ai-grok\";\nimport { audioFile } from \"./audio\";\n\nconst result = await generateTranscription({\n  adapter: grokTranscription(\"grok-stt\"),\n  audio: audioFile,\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.text);","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"realtime-voice","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Realtime Voice"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Grok also exposes a Realtime voice adapter ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grokRealtime"},{"type":"text","value":") and a token issuer ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grokRealtimeToken"},{"type":"text","value":") for low-latency voice conversations. The default model is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grok-voice-think-fast-2.0"},{"type":"text","value":" (xAI's current recommended speech-to-speech model); "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grok-voice-latest"},{"type":"text","value":" always points at the newest model. The 1.0 ids remain accepted for compatibility, but xAI has deprecated "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grok-voice-think-fast-1.0"},{"type":"text","value":". See "},{"type":"link","href":"../media/realtime-chat","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Realtime Voice Chat"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for the end-to-end flow."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"environment-variables","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Environment Variables"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Set your API key in environment variables:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"XAI_API_KEY=xai-...","lang":"bash"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"implementation-notes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Implementation Notes"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"responses-api","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Responses API"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Grok text and summarize adapters use xAI's "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Responses API"}]},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/v1/responses"},{"type":"text","value":"). Requests default to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"store: false"},{"type":"text","value":" and include encrypted reasoning content with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"include: [\"reasoning.encrypted_content\"]"},{"type":"text","value":"; both can be overridden through "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The shared Responses implementation supports streaming text, reasoning events, structured output via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"text.format"},{"type":"text","value":", and user-defined function tools."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"api-reference","children":[{"type":"text","value":"API Reference"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"groktext-model-config","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grokText(model, config?)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates a Grok text adapter using environment variables."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters:"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"model"},{"type":"text","value":" - The model name ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'grok-4.3'"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'grok-build-0.1'"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"config.baseURL?"},{"type":"text","value":" - Custom base URL (optional)"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" A Grok text adapter instance."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"creategroktext-model-apikey-config","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createGrokText(model, apiKey, config?)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates a Grok text adapter with an explicit API key."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters:"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"model"},{"type":"text","value":" - The model name"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"apiKey"},{"type":"text","value":" - Your xAI API key"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"config.baseURL?"},{"type":"text","value":" - Custom base URL (optional)"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" A Grok text adapter instance."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"groksummarize-model-config","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grokSummarize(model, config?)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates a Grok summarization adapter using environment variables."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" A Grok summarize adapter instance."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"creategroksummarize-model-apikey-config","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createGrokSummarize(model, apiKey, config?)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates a Grok summarization adapter with an explicit API key."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" A Grok summarize adapter instance."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"grokimage-model-config-creategrokimage-model-apikey-config","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grokImage(model, config?)"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createGrokImage(model, apiKey, config?)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates a Grok image generation adapter."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"grokvideo-model-config-creategrokvideo-model-apikey-config","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grokVideo(model, config?)"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createGrokVideo(model, apiKey, config?)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates a Grok video generation adapter (experimental) for the Grok Imagine video models ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'grok-imagine-video'"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'grok-imagine-video-1.5'"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"grokspeech-model-config-creategrokspeech-model-apikey-config","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grokSpeech(model, config?)"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createGrokSpeech(model, apiKey, config?)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates a Grok text-to-speech adapter."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"groktranscription-model-config-creategroktranscription-model-apikey-config","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grokTranscription(model, config?)"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createGrokTranscription(model, apiKey, config?)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates a Grok speech-to-text adapter."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"grokrealtime-grokrealtimetoken","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grokRealtime(...)"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grokRealtimeToken(...)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Realtime voice adapter and token issuer. See "},{"type":"link","href":"../media/realtime-chat","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Realtime Voice Chat"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for usage."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"next-steps","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Next Steps"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../getting-started/quick-start","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Getting Started"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Learn the basics"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../tools/tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tools Guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Learn about tools"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./openai","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Other Adapters"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Explore other providers"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"provider-tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provider Tools"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Grok does not currently expose provider-specific tool factories.\nDefine your own tools with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolDefinition()"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See "},{"type":"link","href":"../tools/tools.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tools"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for the general tool-definition flow, or\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../tools/provider-tools.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provider Tools"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for other providers'\nnative-tool offerings."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"installation","text":"Installation","level":2},{"id":"basic-usage","text":"Basic Usage","level":2},{"id":"basic-usage-custom-api-key","text":"Basic Usage - Custom API Key","level":2},{"id":"configuration","text":"Configuration","level":2},{"id":"grok-on-vertex","text":"Grok on Vertex","level":2},{"id":"example-chat-completion","text":"Example: Chat Completion","level":2},{"id":"example-with-tools","text":"Example: With Tools","level":2},{"id":"model-options","text":"Model Options","level":2},{"id":"summarization","text":"Summarization","level":2},{"id":"image-generation","text":"Image Generation","level":2},{"id":"image-editing-image-to-image","text":"Image Editing (image-to-image)","level":3},{"id":"video-generation-experimental","text":"Video Generation (Experimental)","level":2},{"id":"reference-to-video","text":"Reference-to-Video","level":3},{"id":"video-editing-and-extension","text":"Video Editing and Extension","level":3},{"id":"text-to-speech","text":"Text-to-Speech","level":2},{"id":"transcription","text":"Transcription","level":2},{"id":"realtime-voice","text":"Realtime Voice","level":2},{"id":"environment-variables","text":"Environment Variables","level":2},{"id":"implementation-notes","text":"Implementation Notes","level":2},{"id":"responses-api","text":"Responses API","level":3},{"id":"api-reference","text":"API Reference","level":2},{"id":"groktext-model-config","text":"grokText(model, config?)","level":3},{"id":"creategroktext-model-apikey-config","text":"createGrokText(model, apiKey, config?)","level":3},{"id":"groksummarize-model-config","text":"grokSummarize(model, config?)","level":3},{"id":"creategroksummarize-model-apikey-config","text":"createGrokSummarize(model, apiKey, config?)","level":3},{"id":"grokimage-model-config-creategrokimage-model-apikey-config","text":"grokImage(model, config?) / createGrokImage(model, apiKey, config?)","level":3},{"id":"grokvideo-model-config-creategrokvideo-model-apikey-config","text":"grokVideo(model, config?) / createGrokVideo(model, apiKey, config?)","level":3},{"id":"grokspeech-model-config-creategrokspeech-model-apikey-config","text":"grokSpeech(model, config?) / createGrokSpeech(model, apiKey, config?)","level":3},{"id":"groktranscription-model-config-creategroktranscription-model-apikey-config","text":"grokTranscription(model, config?) / createGrokTranscription(model, apiKey, config?)","level":3},{"id":"grokrealtime-grokrealtimetoken","text":"grokRealtime(...) / grokRealtimeToken(...)","level":3},{"id":"next-steps","text":"Next Steps","level":2},{"id":"provider-tools","text":"Provider Tools","level":2}]},"frameworks":["react","vue","solid","svelte","preact","angular","vanilla","octane"],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThe Grok text and summarization adapters provide access to xAI's Responses API for `grok-4.3` and `grok-build-0.1`, plus Grok Imagine image generation and Grok Imagine video generation.\n\n## Installation\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-grok\nvue: @tanstack/ai-grok\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-grok\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-grok\npreact: @tanstack/ai-grok\nangular: @tanstack/ai-grok\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-grok\noctane: @tanstack/ai-grok\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n## Basic Usage\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { grokText } from \"@tanstack/ai-grok\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: grokText(\"grok-build-0.1\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello!\" }],\n});\n```\n\n## Basic Usage - Custom API Key\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { createGrokText } from \"@tanstack/ai-grok\";\n\nconst adapter = createGrokText(\"grok-build-0.1\", process.env.XAI_API_KEY!);\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter,\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello!\" }],\n});\n```\n\n## Configuration\n\n```typescript\nimport { createGrokText, type GrokTextConfig } from \"@tanstack/ai-grok\";\n\nconst config: Omit<GrokTextConfig, \"apiKey\"> = {\n  baseURL: \"https://api.x.ai/v1\", // Optional, this is the default\n};\n\nconst adapter = createGrokText(\"grok-build-0.1\", process.env.XAI_API_KEY!, config);\n```\n\n## Grok on Vertex\n\nUse `@tanstack/ai-grok/vertex` when Grok must run on Vertex AI. That path\nuses Google Cloud credentials and Vertex regional or global endpoints.\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-grok google-auth-library\nvue: @tanstack/ai-grok google-auth-library\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-grok google-auth-library\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-grok google-auth-library\npreact: @tanstack/ai-grok google-auth-library\nangular: @tanstack/ai-grok google-auth-library\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-grok google-auth-library\noctane: @tanstack/ai-grok google-auth-library\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { grokVertexText } from \"@tanstack/ai-grok/vertex\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: grokVertexText(\"grok-4.3\", {\n    project: \"my-project\",\n    location: \"global\",\n  }),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello!\" }],\n});\n```\n\n`project` and `location` use the same names as `@tanstack/ai-vertex`. If you\nomit `location`, the factory uses `global`.\n\n`grokVertexText` accepts only the Grok chat models that Vertex lists:\n\n- `grok-4.3`\n- `grok-4.20-reasoning`\n- `grok-4.20-non-reasoning`\n- `grok-4.1-fast-reasoning`\n- `grok-4.1-fast-non-reasoning`\n\nxAI API models such as `grok-4.6` and `grok-build-0.1` are not on Vertex.\n\nThe adapter sends the Vertex model id `xai/grok-4.3`. Install\n`google-auth-library` for Application Default Credentials, or pass\n`authClient` or `getAccessToken`.\n\nUse `grokVertexSummarize` from the same entry when you need summarize on\nVertex.\n\nGemini on Vertex lives in [`@tanstack/ai-vertex`](./vertex).\n\n## Example: Chat Completion\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { grokText } from \"@tanstack/ai-grok\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json();\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: grokText(\"grok-build-0.1\"),\n    messages,\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}\n```\n\n## Example: With Tools\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse, toolDefinition } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { grokText } from \"@tanstack/ai-grok\";\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\n\nconst getWeatherDef = toolDefinition({\n  name: \"get_weather\",\n  description: \"Get the current weather\",\n  inputSchema: z.object({\n    location: z.string(),\n  }),\n});\n\nconst getWeather = getWeatherDef.server(async ({ location }) => {\n  // Fetch weather data\n  return { temperature: 72, conditions: \"sunny\" };\n});\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json();\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: grokText(\"grok-build-0.1\"),\n    messages,\n    tools: [getWeather],\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}\n```\n\n## Model Options\n\nGrok supports xAI Responses API options. Sampling parameters live here too — `temperature`, `top_p`, and `max_output_tokens` — rather than as root-level props on `chat()`:\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { grokText } from \"@tanstack/ai-grok\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json();\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: grokText(\"grok-build-0.1\"),\n    messages,\n    modelOptions: {\n      temperature: 0.7,\n      top_p: 0.9,\n      max_output_tokens: 1024,\n      store: false,\n      include: [\"reasoning.encrypted_content\"],\n    },\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}\n```\n\n> If you previously passed `temperature` / `topP` / `maxTokens` at the root of `chat()`, see [Moving Sampling Options into modelOptions](../migration/sampling-options-to-model-options).\n\n## Summarization\n\nSummarize long text content:\n\n<!-- ignored: grokSummarize()'s resolved provider-options type sits in a\n     contravariant position in SummarizeAdapter, so it isn't assignable to\n     summarize()'s adapter param for any current Grok model. Tracked in #821;\n     un-ignore once the adapter type is corrected. -->\n\n```typescript ignore\nimport { summarize } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { grokSummarize } from \"@tanstack/ai-grok\";\n\nconst result = await summarize({\n  adapter: grokSummarize(\"grok-4.3\"),\n  text: \"Your long text to summarize...\",\n  maxLength: 100,\n  style: \"concise\", // \"concise\" | \"bullet-points\" | \"paragraph\"\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.summary);\n```\n\n## Image Generation\n\nGenerate images with a Grok Imagine model.\n\nThe image models (`grok-imagine-image`, `grok-imagine-image-2.0`,\n`grok-imagine-image-quality`) are aspect-ratio sized — `size` takes an\n`aspectRatio_resolution` template like `\"16:9_2k\"` (the `_2k` suffix is\noptional). `grok-imagine-image-2.0` is xAI's recommended model and adds a\n2.0-only `quality` provider option (`'low' | 'medium'`, default `'medium'`):\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { grokImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-grok\";\n\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: grokImage(\"grok-imagine-image-2.0\"),\n  prompt: \"A futuristic cityscape at sunset\",\n  size: \"16:9_2k\",\n  modelOptions: { quality: \"medium\" },\n});\n```\n\n### Image Editing (image-to-image)\n\nThe grok-imagine models accept image prompt parts for image-conditioned\ngeneration via xAI's `/v1/images/edits` endpoint — up to 3 source images,\naddressed by xAI in the order they appear in the prompt. Per xAI's docs\nthere is no in-prompt referencing syntax; write the prompt naturally and\nyour text is sent verbatim:\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { grokImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-grok\";\n\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: grokImage(\"grok-imagine-image\"),\n  prompt: [\n    {\n      type: \"text\",\n      content: \"Render the product in the style of the second image\",\n    },\n    {\n      type: \"image\",\n      source: { type: \"url\", value: \"https://example.com/product.png\" },\n    },\n    {\n      type: \"image\",\n      source: { type: \"url\", value: \"https://example.com/style.png\" },\n    },\n  ],\n});\n```\n\nURL sources are fetched by xAI's servers, so they must be publicly\nreachable; use a `data` source for private images.\n\n## Video Generation (Experimental)\n\nGenerate short video clips (1–15 seconds, with audio) with the Grok Imagine video models via xAI's asynchronous jobs/polling API.\n\nAvailable models:\n\n- `grok-imagine-video` (v1.0) — text-to-video, image-to-video, and source-video edit / extend, $0.05 per second of video.\n- `grok-imagine-video-1.5` — xAI's recommended default, $0.08 per second of video. Supports text-to-video (with native 1080p), image-to-video, and reference-to-video. It does not accept a source video.\n\nText-to-video:\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateVideo, getVideoJobStatus } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { grokVideo } from \"@tanstack/ai-grok\";\n\nconst adapter = grokVideo(\"grok-imagine-video-1.5\");\n\n// 1. Create the job\nconst { jobId } = await generateVideo({\n  adapter,\n  prompt: \"A red panda balancing on a bamboo stalk in the rain\",\n  size: \"16:9_720p\", // \"aspectRatio\" or \"aspectRatio_resolution\"\n  duration: 5, // integer seconds, 1–15\n});\n\n// 2. Poll until complete, then read the video URL\nlet status = await getVideoJobStatus({ adapter, jobId });\nwhile (status.status !== \"completed\" && status.status !== \"failed\") {\n  await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, 5000));\n  status = await getVideoJobStatus({ adapter, jobId });\n}\n\nconsole.log(status.url); // hosted .mp4 URL\n```\n\nFor image-to-video, include an `image` prompt part as the starting frame and describe the desired motion in the text part. URL sources are fetched by xAI's servers (so they must be publicly reachable); use a `data` source for a base64 starting frame:\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateVideo } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { grokVideo } from \"@tanstack/ai-grok\";\n\nconst { jobId } = await generateVideo({\n  adapter: grokVideo(\"grok-imagine-video-1.5\"),\n  prompt: [\n    {\n      type: \"text\",\n      content: \"Make the waterfall crash down and slowly pan out the camera\",\n    },\n    {\n      type: \"image\",\n      source: { type: \"url\", value: \"https://example.com/waterfall-still.png\" },\n    },\n  ],\n  size: \"16:9_720p\",\n  duration: 10,\n});\n```\n\nLike the Grok Imagine image models, sizing is aspect-ratio based: the `size` option takes an `aspectRatio_resolution` template. Supported aspect ratios are `1:1`, `16:9`, `9:16`, `4:3`, `3:4`, `3:2`, and `2:3`; supported resolutions are `480p`, `720p`, and (on `grok-imagine-video-1.5` text-to-video / image-to-video only) `1080p` (e.g. `\"9:16_1080p\"`). The resolution suffix is optional.\n\n### Reference-to-Video\n\nOn `grok-imagine-video-1.5`, image prompt parts with `metadata.role: 'reference'` (or `'character'`) become `reference_images` — they guide subjects and style without locking the first frame, and are addressed from the prompt text as `<IMAGE_0>`, `<IMAGE_1>`, … in request order. Preset TTS voices (up to 3) can be referenced for generated speech via `modelOptions.reference_audios`, addressed as `<AUDIO_0>`, `<AUDIO_1>`, `<AUDIO_2>`. Reference-to-video output is capped at 720p. A starting-frame image can be combined with reference inputs on 1.5: the start frame pins the opening frame while the references steer subjects, style, and voices. Reference inputs are a 1.5-only feature, so the adapter rejects them on `grok-imagine-video`:\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateVideo } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { grokVideo } from \"@tanstack/ai-grok\";\n\nconst { jobId } = await generateVideo({\n  adapter: grokVideo(\"grok-imagine-video-1.5\"),\n  prompt: [\n    {\n      type: \"text\",\n      content: \"<IMAGE_0> walks through a neon-lit alley while <AUDIO_0> narrates\",\n    },\n    {\n      type: \"image\",\n      source: { type: \"url\", value: \"https://example.com/opening-frame.png\" },\n      metadata: { role: \"start_frame\" },\n    },\n    {\n      type: \"image\",\n      source: { type: \"url\", value: \"https://example.com/character.png\" },\n      metadata: { role: \"reference\" },\n    },\n  ],\n  size: \"16:9_720p\",\n  modelOptions: {\n    reference_audios: [{ voice_id: \"eve\" }],\n  },\n});\n```\n\n### Video Editing and Extension\n\n`grok-imagine-video` (v1.0) can rewrite or continue an existing clip. `grok-imagine-video-1.5` has no video input — the adapter rejects a source-video part or `mode` on that model. Pass the source clip as a `video` prompt part and pick the mode with `modelOptions.mode`:\n\n- `mode: 'edit'` posts to `/v1/videos/edits` — modifies only what the prompt asks for, keeping the rest of the clip intact. Duration, aspect ratio, and resolution are inherited from the source (capped at 720p), so the adapter rejects `size`, `aspect_ratio`, `resolution`, and `duration` in this mode rather than sending fields the API ignores.\n- `mode: 'extend'` posts to `/v1/videos/extensions` — continues the clip. `duration` is the length of the **added tail**, not the total: extending a 10-second clip with `duration: 5` yields 15 seconds. Output geometry is still inherited from the source, so `size` / `aspect_ratio` / `resolution` are rejected here too.\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateVideo } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { grokVideo } from \"@tanstack/ai-grok\";\n\nconst adapter = grokVideo(\"grok-imagine-video\");\n\n// Edit: change the clip in place\nconst edit = await generateVideo({\n  adapter,\n  prompt: [\n    { type: \"text\", content: \"Make the sky stormy with distant lightning\" },\n    {\n      type: \"video\",\n      source: { type: \"url\", value: \"https://example.com/clip.mp4\" },\n    },\n  ],\n  modelOptions: { mode: \"edit\" },\n});\n\n// Extend: append 5 more seconds\nconst extension = await generateVideo({\n  adapter,\n  prompt: [\n    { type: \"text\", content: \"The camera keeps panning right across the bay\" },\n    {\n      type: \"video\",\n      source: { type: \"url\", value: \"https://example.com/clip.mp4\" },\n    },\n  ],\n  duration: 5, // added seconds, not the total\n  modelOptions: { mode: \"extend\" },\n});\n```\n\nBoth return the usual `{ jobId }` and are polled like any other Grok video job.\n\nWhen the job completes, the adapter reports usage on the result: `usage.billed` carries the billed seconds of video (`{ quantity, unit: 'seconds' }`) and `usage.cost` the exact cost in USD, both as returned by the xAI API.\n\nSee [Video Generation](../media/video-generation) for the full jobs/polling flow, streaming mode, and the `useGenerateVideo` hook.\n\n## Text-to-Speech\n\nGenerate speech with Grok TTS:\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateSpeech } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { grokSpeech } from \"@tanstack/ai-grok\";\n\nconst result = await generateSpeech({\n  adapter: grokSpeech(\"grok-tts\"),\n  text: \"Hello from Grok!\",\n  voice: \"default\",\n  format: \"mp3\",\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.audio); // Base64-encoded audio\n```\n\n## Transcription\n\nTranscribe audio with Grok STT:\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateTranscription } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { grokTranscription } from \"@tanstack/ai-grok\";\nimport { audioFile } from \"./audio\";\n\nconst result = await generateTranscription({\n  adapter: grokTranscription(\"grok-stt\"),\n  audio: audioFile,\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.text);\n```\n\n## Realtime Voice\n\nGrok also exposes a Realtime voice adapter (`grokRealtime`) and a token issuer (`grokRealtimeToken`) for low-latency voice conversations. The default model is `grok-voice-think-fast-2.0` (xAI's current recommended speech-to-speech model); `grok-voice-latest` always points at the newest model. The 1.0 ids remain accepted for compatibility, but xAI has deprecated `grok-voice-think-fast-1.0`. See [Realtime Voice Chat](../media/realtime-chat) for the end-to-end flow.\n\n## Environment Variables\n\nSet your API key in environment variables:\n\n```bash\nXAI_API_KEY=xai-...\n```\n\n## Implementation Notes\n\n### Responses API\n\nThe Grok text and summarize adapters use xAI's **Responses API** (`/v1/responses`). Requests default to `store: false` and include encrypted reasoning content with `include: [\"reasoning.encrypted_content\"]`; both can be overridden through `modelOptions`.\n\nThe shared Responses implementation supports streaming text, reasoning events, structured output via `text.format`, and user-defined function tools.\n\n## API Reference\n\n### `grokText(model, config?)`\n\nCreates a Grok text adapter using environment variables.\n\n**Parameters:**\n\n- `model` - The model name (`'grok-4.3'` or `'grok-build-0.1'`)\n- `config.baseURL?` - Custom base URL (optional)\n\n**Returns:** A Grok text adapter instance.\n\n### `createGrokText(model, apiKey, config?)`\n\nCreates a Grok text adapter with an explicit API key.\n\n**Parameters:**\n\n- `model` - The model name\n- `apiKey` - Your xAI API key\n- `config.baseURL?` - Custom base URL (optional)\n\n**Returns:** A Grok text adapter instance.\n\n### `grokSummarize(model, config?)`\n\nCreates a Grok summarization adapter using environment variables.\n\n**Returns:** A Grok summarize adapter instance.\n\n### `createGrokSummarize(model, apiKey, config?)`\n\nCreates a Grok summarization adapter with an explicit API key.\n\n**Returns:** A Grok summarize adapter instance.\n\n### `grokImage(model, config?)` / `createGrokImage(model, apiKey, config?)`\n\nCreates a Grok image generation adapter.\n\n### `grokVideo(model, config?)` / `createGrokVideo(model, apiKey, config?)`\n\nCreates a Grok video generation adapter (experimental) for the Grok Imagine video models (`'grok-imagine-video'`, `'grok-imagine-video-1.5'`).\n\n### `grokSpeech(model, config?)` / `createGrokSpeech(model, apiKey, config?)`\n\nCreates a Grok text-to-speech adapter.\n\n### `grokTranscription(model, config?)` / `createGrokTranscription(model, apiKey, config?)`\n\nCreates a Grok speech-to-text adapter.\n\n### `grokRealtime(...)` / `grokRealtimeToken(...)`\n\nRealtime voice adapter and token issuer. See [Realtime Voice Chat](../media/realtime-chat) for usage.\n\n## Next Steps\n\n- [Getting Started](../getting-started/quick-start) - Learn the basics\n- [Tools Guide](../tools/tools) - Learn about tools\n- [Other Adapters](./openai) - Explore other providers\n\n## Provider Tools\n\nGrok does not currently expose provider-specific tool factories.\nDefine your own tools with `toolDefinition()` from `@tanstack/ai`.\n\nSee [Tools](../tools/tools.md) for the general tool-definition flow, or\n[Provider Tools](../tools/provider-tools.md) for other providers'\nnative-tool offerings.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Grok (xAI)\nid: grok-adapter\norder: 5\ndescription: \"Use xAI Grok models with TanStack AI — Grok 4.3, Grok Build 0.1, Grok Imagine image generation, and Grok Imagine video generation via @tanstack/ai-grok.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - grok\n  - xai\n  - grok 4.3\n  - grok build\n  - image generation\n  - video generation\n  - grok imagine\n  - adapter\n---\n\nThe Grok text and summarization adapters provide access to xAI's Responses API for `grok-4.3` and `grok-build-0.1`, plus Grok Imagine image generation and Grok Imagine video generation.\n\n## Installation\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-grok\nvue: @tanstack/ai-grok\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-grok\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-grok\npreact: @tanstack/ai-grok\nangular: @tanstack/ai-grok\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-grok\noctane: @tanstack/ai-grok\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n## Basic Usage\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { grokText } from \"@tanstack/ai-grok\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: grokText(\"grok-build-0.1\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello!\" }],\n});\n```\n\n## Basic Usage - Custom API Key\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { createGrokText } from \"@tanstack/ai-grok\";\n\nconst adapter = createGrokText(\"grok-build-0.1\", process.env.XAI_API_KEY!);\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter,\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello!\" }],\n});\n```\n\n## Configuration\n\n```typescript\nimport { createGrokText, type GrokTextConfig } from \"@tanstack/ai-grok\";\n\nconst config: Omit<GrokTextConfig, \"apiKey\"> = {\n  baseURL: \"https://api.x.ai/v1\", // Optional, this is the default\n};\n\nconst adapter = createGrokText(\"grok-build-0.1\", process.env.XAI_API_KEY!, config);\n```\n\n## Grok on Vertex\n\nUse `@tanstack/ai-grok/vertex` when Grok must run on Vertex AI. That path\nuses Google Cloud credentials and Vertex regional or global endpoints.\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-grok google-auth-library\nvue: @tanstack/ai-grok google-auth-library\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-grok google-auth-library\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-grok google-auth-library\npreact: @tanstack/ai-grok google-auth-library\nangular: @tanstack/ai-grok google-auth-library\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-grok google-auth-library\noctane: @tanstack/ai-grok google-auth-library\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { grokVertexText } from \"@tanstack/ai-grok/vertex\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: grokVertexText(\"grok-4.3\", {\n    project: \"my-project\",\n    location: \"global\",\n  }),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello!\" }],\n});\n```\n\n`project` and `location` use the same names as `@tanstack/ai-vertex`. If you\nomit `location`, the factory uses `global`.\n\n`grokVertexText` accepts only the Grok chat models that Vertex lists:\n\n- `grok-4.3`\n- `grok-4.20-reasoning`\n- `grok-4.20-non-reasoning`\n- `grok-4.1-fast-reasoning`\n- `grok-4.1-fast-non-reasoning`\n\nxAI API models such as `grok-4.6` and `grok-build-0.1` are not on Vertex.\n\nThe adapter sends the Vertex model id `xai/grok-4.3`. Install\n`google-auth-library` for Application Default Credentials, or pass\n`authClient` or `getAccessToken`.\n\nUse `grokVertexSummarize` from the same entry when you need summarize on\nVertex.\n\nGemini on Vertex lives in [`@tanstack/ai-vertex`](./vertex).\n\n## Example: Chat Completion\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { grokText } from \"@tanstack/ai-grok\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json();\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: grokText(\"grok-build-0.1\"),\n    messages,\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}\n```\n\n## Example: With Tools\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse, toolDefinition } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { grokText } from \"@tanstack/ai-grok\";\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\n\nconst getWeatherDef = toolDefinition({\n  name: \"get_weather\",\n  description: \"Get the current weather\",\n  inputSchema: z.object({\n    location: z.string(),\n  }),\n});\n\nconst getWeather = getWeatherDef.server(async ({ location }) => {\n  // Fetch weather data\n  return { temperature: 72, conditions: \"sunny\" };\n});\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json();\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: grokText(\"grok-build-0.1\"),\n    messages,\n    tools: [getWeather],\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}\n```\n\n## Model Options\n\nGrok supports xAI Responses API options. Sampling parameters live here too — `temperature`, `top_p`, and `max_output_tokens` — rather than as root-level props on `chat()`:\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { grokText } from \"@tanstack/ai-grok\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json();\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: grokText(\"grok-build-0.1\"),\n    messages,\n    modelOptions: {\n      temperature: 0.7,\n      top_p: 0.9,\n      max_output_tokens: 1024,\n      store: false,\n      include: [\"reasoning.encrypted_content\"],\n    },\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}\n```\n\n> If you previously passed `temperature` / `topP` / `maxTokens` at the root of `chat()`, see [Moving Sampling Options into modelOptions](../migration/sampling-options-to-model-options).\n\n## Summarization\n\nSummarize long text content:\n\n<!-- ignored: grokSummarize()'s resolved provider-options type sits in a\n     contravariant position in SummarizeAdapter, so it isn't assignable to\n     summarize()'s adapter param for any current Grok model. Tracked in #821;\n     un-ignore once the adapter type is corrected. -->\n\n```typescript ignore\nimport { summarize } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { grokSummarize } from \"@tanstack/ai-grok\";\n\nconst result = await summarize({\n  adapter: grokSummarize(\"grok-4.3\"),\n  text: \"Your long text to summarize...\",\n  maxLength: 100,\n  style: \"concise\", // \"concise\" | \"bullet-points\" | \"paragraph\"\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.summary);\n```\n\n## Image Generation\n\nGenerate images with a Grok Imagine model.\n\nThe image models (`grok-imagine-image`, `grok-imagine-image-2.0`,\n`grok-imagine-image-quality`) are aspect-ratio sized — `size` takes an\n`aspectRatio_resolution` template like `\"16:9_2k\"` (the `_2k` suffix is\noptional). `grok-imagine-image-2.0` is xAI's recommended model and adds a\n2.0-only `quality` provider option (`'low' | 'medium'`, default `'medium'`):\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { grokImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-grok\";\n\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: grokImage(\"grok-imagine-image-2.0\"),\n  prompt: \"A futuristic cityscape at sunset\",\n  size: \"16:9_2k\",\n  modelOptions: { quality: \"medium\" },\n});\n```\n\n### Image Editing (image-to-image)\n\nThe grok-imagine models accept image prompt parts for image-conditioned\ngeneration via xAI's `/v1/images/edits` endpoint — up to 3 source images,\naddressed by xAI in the order they appear in the prompt. Per xAI's docs\nthere is no in-prompt referencing syntax; write the prompt naturally and\nyour text is sent verbatim:\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { grokImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-grok\";\n\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: grokImage(\"grok-imagine-image\"),\n  prompt: [\n    {\n      type: \"text\",\n      content: \"Render the product in the style of the second image\",\n    },\n    {\n      type: \"image\",\n      source: { type: \"url\", value: \"https://example.com/product.png\" },\n    },\n    {\n      type: \"image\",\n      source: { type: \"url\", value: \"https://example.com/style.png\" },\n    },\n  ],\n});\n```\n\nURL sources are fetched by xAI's servers, so they must be publicly\nreachable; use a `data` source for private images.\n\n## Video Generation (Experimental)\n\nGenerate short video clips (1–15 seconds, with audio) with the Grok Imagine video models via xAI's asynchronous jobs/polling API.\n\nAvailable models:\n\n- `grok-imagine-video` (v1.0) — text-to-video, image-to-video, and source-video edit / extend, $0.05 per second of video.\n- `grok-imagine-video-1.5` — xAI's recommended default, $0.08 per second of video. Supports text-to-video (with native 1080p), image-to-video, and reference-to-video. It does not accept a source video.\n\nText-to-video:\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateVideo, getVideoJobStatus } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { grokVideo } from \"@tanstack/ai-grok\";\n\nconst adapter = grokVideo(\"grok-imagine-video-1.5\");\n\n// 1. Create the job\nconst { jobId } = await generateVideo({\n  adapter,\n  prompt: \"A red panda balancing on a bamboo stalk in the rain\",\n  size: \"16:9_720p\", // \"aspectRatio\" or \"aspectRatio_resolution\"\n  duration: 5, // integer seconds, 1–15\n});\n\n// 2. Poll until complete, then read the video URL\nlet status = await getVideoJobStatus({ adapter, jobId });\nwhile (status.status !== \"completed\" && status.status !== \"failed\") {\n  await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, 5000));\n  status = await getVideoJobStatus({ adapter, jobId });\n}\n\nconsole.log(status.url); // hosted .mp4 URL\n```\n\nFor image-to-video, include an `image` prompt part as the starting frame and describe the desired motion in the text part. URL sources are fetched by xAI's servers (so they must be publicly reachable); use a `data` source for a base64 starting frame:\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateVideo } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { grokVideo } from \"@tanstack/ai-grok\";\n\nconst { jobId } = await generateVideo({\n  adapter: grokVideo(\"grok-imagine-video-1.5\"),\n  prompt: [\n    {\n      type: \"text\",\n      content: \"Make the waterfall crash down and slowly pan out the camera\",\n    },\n    {\n      type: \"image\",\n      source: { type: \"url\", value: \"https://example.com/waterfall-still.png\" },\n    },\n  ],\n  size: \"16:9_720p\",\n  duration: 10,\n});\n```\n\nLike the Grok Imagine image models, sizing is aspect-ratio based: the `size` option takes an `aspectRatio_resolution` template. Supported aspect ratios are `1:1`, `16:9`, `9:16`, `4:3`, `3:4`, `3:2`, and `2:3`; supported resolutions are `480p`, `720p`, and (on `grok-imagine-video-1.5` text-to-video / image-to-video only) `1080p` (e.g. `\"9:16_1080p\"`). The resolution suffix is optional.\n\n### Reference-to-Video\n\nOn `grok-imagine-video-1.5`, image prompt parts with `metadata.role: 'reference'` (or `'character'`) become `reference_images` — they guide subjects and style without locking the first frame, and are addressed from the prompt text as `<IMAGE_0>`, `<IMAGE_1>`, … in request order. Preset TTS voices (up to 3) can be referenced for generated speech via `modelOptions.reference_audios`, addressed as `<AUDIO_0>`, `<AUDIO_1>`, `<AUDIO_2>`. Reference-to-video output is capped at 720p. A starting-frame image can be combined with reference inputs on 1.5: the start frame pins the opening frame while the references steer subjects, style, and voices. Reference inputs are a 1.5-only feature, so the adapter rejects them on `grok-imagine-video`:\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateVideo } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { grokVideo } from \"@tanstack/ai-grok\";\n\nconst { jobId } = await generateVideo({\n  adapter: grokVideo(\"grok-imagine-video-1.5\"),\n  prompt: [\n    {\n      type: \"text\",\n      content: \"<IMAGE_0> walks through a neon-lit alley while <AUDIO_0> narrates\",\n    },\n    {\n      type: \"image\",\n      source: { type: \"url\", value: \"https://example.com/opening-frame.png\" },\n      metadata: { role: \"start_frame\" },\n    },\n    {\n      type: \"image\",\n      source: { type: \"url\", value: \"https://example.com/character.png\" },\n      metadata: { role: \"reference\" },\n    },\n  ],\n  size: \"16:9_720p\",\n  modelOptions: {\n    reference_audios: [{ voice_id: \"eve\" }],\n  },\n});\n```\n\n### Video Editing and Extension\n\n`grok-imagine-video` (v1.0) can rewrite or continue an existing clip. `grok-imagine-video-1.5` has no video input — the adapter rejects a source-video part or `mode` on that model. Pass the source clip as a `video` prompt part and pick the mode with `modelOptions.mode`:\n\n- `mode: 'edit'` posts to `/v1/videos/edits` — modifies only what the prompt asks for, keeping the rest of the clip intact. Duration, aspect ratio, and resolution are inherited from the source (capped at 720p), so the adapter rejects `size`, `aspect_ratio`, `resolution`, and `duration` in this mode rather than sending fields the API ignores.\n- `mode: 'extend'` posts to `/v1/videos/extensions` — continues the clip. `duration` is the length of the **added tail**, not the total: extending a 10-second clip with `duration: 5` yields 15 seconds. Output geometry is still inherited from the source, so `size` / `aspect_ratio` / `resolution` are rejected here too.\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateVideo } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { grokVideo } from \"@tanstack/ai-grok\";\n\nconst adapter = grokVideo(\"grok-imagine-video\");\n\n// Edit: change the clip in place\nconst edit = await generateVideo({\n  adapter,\n  prompt: [\n    { type: \"text\", content: \"Make the sky stormy with distant lightning\" },\n    {\n      type: \"video\",\n      source: { type: \"url\", value: \"https://example.com/clip.mp4\" },\n    },\n  ],\n  modelOptions: { mode: \"edit\" },\n});\n\n// Extend: append 5 more seconds\nconst extension = await generateVideo({\n  adapter,\n  prompt: [\n    { type: \"text\", content: \"The camera keeps panning right across the bay\" },\n    {\n      type: \"video\",\n      source: { type: \"url\", value: \"https://example.com/clip.mp4\" },\n    },\n  ],\n  duration: 5, // added seconds, not the total\n  modelOptions: { mode: \"extend\" },\n});\n```\n\nBoth return the usual `{ jobId }` and are polled like any other Grok video job.\n\nWhen the job completes, the adapter reports usage on the result: `usage.billed` carries the billed seconds of video (`{ quantity, unit: 'seconds' }`) and `usage.cost` the exact cost in USD, both as returned by the xAI API.\n\nSee [Video Generation](../media/video-generation) for the full jobs/polling flow, streaming mode, and the `useGenerateVideo` hook.\n\n## Text-to-Speech\n\nGenerate speech with Grok TTS:\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateSpeech } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { grokSpeech } from \"@tanstack/ai-grok\";\n\nconst result = await generateSpeech({\n  adapter: grokSpeech(\"grok-tts\"),\n  text: \"Hello from Grok!\",\n  voice: \"default\",\n  format: \"mp3\",\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.audio); // Base64-encoded audio\n```\n\n## Transcription\n\nTranscribe audio with Grok STT:\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateTranscription } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { grokTranscription } from \"@tanstack/ai-grok\";\nimport { audioFile } from \"./audio\";\n\nconst result = await generateTranscription({\n  adapter: grokTranscription(\"grok-stt\"),\n  audio: audioFile,\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.text);\n```\n\n## Realtime Voice\n\nGrok also exposes a Realtime voice adapter (`grokRealtime`) and a token issuer (`grokRealtimeToken`) for low-latency voice conversations. The default model is `grok-voice-think-fast-2.0` (xAI's current recommended speech-to-speech model); `grok-voice-latest` always points at the newest model. The 1.0 ids remain accepted for compatibility, but xAI has deprecated `grok-voice-think-fast-1.0`. See [Realtime Voice Chat](../media/realtime-chat) for the end-to-end flow.\n\n## Environment Variables\n\nSet your API key in environment variables:\n\n```bash\nXAI_API_KEY=xai-...\n```\n\n## Implementation Notes\n\n### Responses API\n\nThe Grok text and summarize adapters use xAI's **Responses API** (`/v1/responses`). Requests default to `store: false` and include encrypted reasoning content with `include: [\"reasoning.encrypted_content\"]`; both can be overridden through `modelOptions`.\n\nThe shared Responses implementation supports streaming text, reasoning events, structured output via `text.format`, and user-defined function tools.\n\n## API Reference\n\n### `grokText(model, config?)`\n\nCreates a Grok text adapter using environment variables.\n\n**Parameters:**\n\n- `model` - The model name (`'grok-4.3'` or `'grok-build-0.1'`)\n- `config.baseURL?` - Custom base URL (optional)\n\n**Returns:** A Grok text adapter instance.\n\n### `createGrokText(model, apiKey, config?)`\n\nCreates a Grok text adapter with an explicit API key.\n\n**Parameters:**\n\n- `model` - The model name\n- `apiKey` - Your xAI API key\n- `config.baseURL?` - Custom base URL (optional)\n\n**Returns:** A Grok text adapter instance.\n\n### `grokSummarize(model, config?)`\n\nCreates a Grok summarization adapter using environment variables.\n\n**Returns:** A Grok summarize adapter instance.\n\n### `createGrokSummarize(model, apiKey, config?)`\n\nCreates a Grok summarization adapter with an explicit API key.\n\n**Returns:** A Grok summarize adapter instance.\n\n### `grokImage(model, config?)` / `createGrokImage(model, apiKey, config?)`\n\nCreates a Grok image generation adapter.\n\n### `grokVideo(model, config?)` / `createGrokVideo(model, apiKey, config?)`\n\nCreates a Grok video generation adapter (experimental) for the Grok Imagine video models (`'grok-imagine-video'`, `'grok-imagine-video-1.5'`).\n\n### `grokSpeech(model, config?)` / `createGrokSpeech(model, apiKey, config?)`\n\nCreates a Grok text-to-speech adapter.\n\n### `grokTranscription(model, config?)` / `createGrokTranscription(model, apiKey, config?)`\n\nCreates a Grok speech-to-text adapter.\n\n### `grokRealtime(...)` / `grokRealtimeToken(...)`\n\nRealtime voice adapter and token issuer. See [Realtime Voice Chat](../media/realtime-chat) for usage.\n\n## Next Steps\n\n- [Getting Started](../getting-started/quick-start) - Learn the basics\n- [Tools Guide](../tools/tools) - Learn about tools\n- [Other Adapters](./openai) - Explore other providers\n\n## Provider Tools\n\nGrok does not currently expose provider-specific tool factories.\nDefine your own tools with `toolDefinition()` from `@tanstack/ai`.\n\nSee [Tools](../tools/tools.md) for the general tool-definition flow, or\n[Provider Tools](../tools/provider-tools.md) for other providers'\nnative-tool offerings.\n"}
